<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caligula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12–41 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Gaius Caesar Augustus Germanicus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caligula, properly Gaius Caesar, was Roman emperor from 37 to 41 CE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a>. Popular at first, his reign became notorious in the ancient sources for cruelty, extravagance and claims to divine honours. He made and remade client kingdoms, giving lands to Herod Agrippa and Polemon II and executing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-of-mauretania">Ptolemy of Mauretania</a>. He was murdered by officers of the Praetorian Guard.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caligula.jpg" alt="Caligula" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergey Sosnovskiy from Saint-Petersburg, Russia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caligula.Carlsberg_Glyptotek.(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Around 39 CE the emperor <b>Caligula</b> transferred command of the legion from the proconsul to an imperial legate, separating the military zone of Numidia from the civil province; the legion moved from Ammaedara to Theveste and finally to Lambaesis, where Hadrian addressed and inspected the troops in 128.</blockquote><a href="/empire/africa-proconsularis">Africa Proconsularis · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Romans installed Mithridates of Armenia, whom <b>Caligula</b> arrested and Claudius restored; the Parthians forced submission in 37 CE, Rome retook the kingdom in 47 CE, Rhadamistus' Iberians seized it in 51 CE and Tigranes VI ruled from 58 CE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-armenia-artaxiad">Kingdom of Armenia (Artaxiad) · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Praetorian officers led by Cassius Chaerea stabbed <b>Caligula</b> in a palace corridor during the Palatine games.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-24">24 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Herod Agrippa I, grandson of Herod the Great and friend of <b>Caligula</b>, received the former Tetrarchy of Philip with the title king in 37.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-herod-agrippa">Kingdom of Herod Agrippa</a></li><li><blockquote>In 40 CE <b>Caligula</b> summoned Juba's son Ptolemy to Rome and had him executed.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-mauretania">Kingdom of Mauretania</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Caligula</b> gave the kingdom to her grandson Polemon II in 38 CE.</blockquote><a href="/state/polemonid-pontus">Polemonid Pontus</a></li></ul></section>
